cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OCF V1 findings, please cite this work."
type: software
title: "Beyond VRAM Capacity: A Single-Workstation Case Study of Strata, Qwen3.8-Flash-Next, and OpenCode on an RTX 5080"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-04"
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Michael
    given-names: Arun C
    affiliation: Independent Systems Engineering Case Study
abstract: >-
  Verified single-workstation systems case study of OCF V1 (OpenCode FlashNext):
  running an 83.62 GB on-disk IQ3_S sparse coding model on an NVIDIA RTX 5080
  (16 GB) via Strata hybrid placement, OpenCode client compaction budgeting, and
  a hardened single-slot FIFO queue. Reports wire-verified compaction latency
  reduction (69.282 s to 18.360 s), direct-NVMe PLE host-RAM savings (~26.8 GiB),
  and deterministic 600 s idle unload with ~30.515 s cold wake.
keywords:
  - local LLM
  - GPU memory hierarchy
  - OpenCode
  - Strata
  - Qwen3.8-Flash-Next
  - OCF V1
  - systems engineering
  - RTX 5080
